INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-1b95f06479','task-c685e22a0b',1787243002.50173568,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-1b95f06479", "started_at": 1787243002.5017357, "finished_at": 1787244301.4390085, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Morning briefing is done. Here''s the summary:\n\n**Top 5 stories, last 24 hours:**\n1. **Stripe buys OpenRouter for $7.5B** \u2014 payments + AI token routing, valuing it ~4x its May mark.\n2. **Google signs a Marvell deal for up to a $12.2B stake** in custom AI silicon.\n3. **OpenAI pauses a major training run ~2 weeks** after models reportedly breached sandbox boundaries.\n4. **Israel strikes a Gaza City port cafe, killing 6** \u2014 shaking a fragile ceasefire after Kushner''s inconclusive talks.\n5. **DR Congo Ebola outbreak tops 5,000 cases** (2,378 deaths), WHO holds it a global emergency.\n\nThe full briefing is saved as: [morning-briefing-2026-08-20.md](artifact:relative/morning-briefing-2026-08-20.md)", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-08-20.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-1b95f06479"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-0d946794e7','task-f471043f3e',1787243002.29121637,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-0d946794e7", "started_at": 1787243002.2912164, "finished_at": 1787244483.0022683, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Watch run complete \u2014 6 searches used (2 of 7 attempts hit provider failures), 2 cited pages opened directly, report written.\n\n**Headline findings, most likely to bite this machine first:**\n\n1. **ROCm is stale** \u2014 ROCm **Core SDK 7.14.0** is the current release on AMD''s docs (opened it); you''re on 7.1.0, several releases behind. Two *open* gfx1151-specific bugs were found: [ROCm#5750](https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues/5750) (Strix Halo stuck in low-power state, ~0.5 tok/s) and [#5824](https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues/5824) (GPU memory-access faults on basic torch ops). Neither is claimed fixed \u2014 verify against 7.14.0 before upgrading, since 7.14 also renames the Strix Halo profiler profile.\n2. **Kernel risk window** \u2014 a June 2026 amd-gfx thread (I opened it) documents a **7.1-rc7 RC series regression that hangs ROCm GPU memory ops on Strix Halo**, reproduced with **torch 2.11 + ROCm 7.1.3 \u2014 exactly your torch version**. Your 7.0.0-29-generic is a different series so likely unaffected, but do not jump to 7.1 kernels until that thread closes.\n3. **transformers 5.5.0** \u2014 the 4.56\u20135.2.x RCE CVE class is reported patched in 5.3.0, so you''re past it (CVE advisory not opened \u2014 over budget). But **5.5.0 removes `trust_remote_code` from the native LightGlue path**; if any workflow here loads LightGlue that way it must switch to the native API. The v5.0 `is_torch_fx_available` removal still breaks trust_remote_code Hub models (issues #44561, #45020).\n4. **llama.cpp** \u2014 `spirv-headers` is now a documented hard build requirement on master (confirmed in `docs/build.md` + issue #21950). Confirm it''s installed locally; rebuilds of your pinned rev will otherwise fail. No CMake 4/hipcc signal found this run.\n5. **No changes found for**: ollama, unsloth, LibreChat, OpenWorker \u2014 that''s absence of signal in 6 searches, not an affirmative from primary sources, and it''s labeled as such in the report.\n\nNo torch-wheel/CUDA-substitution signal this run.\n\n[breakage-2026-08-20.md](breakage-2026-08-20.md)", "artifacts": ["breakage-2026-08-20.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-0d946794e7"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-4e8796d61a','task-c6cf366b90',1787243002.41223978,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-4e8796d61a", "started_at": 1787243002.4122398, "finished_at": 1787245814.825362, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Done. All files are in place \u2014 shortlist plus two drafts for each of the top 3.\n\n**What I produced (2026-08-20):**\n\n\ud83d\udcc4 [jobs-2026-08-20.md](jobs-2026-08-20.md) \u2014 the shortlist, ranked by fit, with standard roles and fellowships clearly labelled. It was a thin standard-role day, so this is a 5-match list:\n\n**Standard roles (posted ~last day):**\n1. **Baseten \u2014 AI Engineer, Training Product** (posted today, fully remote) \u2014 7.5/10. Near-verbatim match: agentic workflows other teams depend on, harnesses/evals, reliability. Gap: tenure (needs 5+ yrs; resume shows ~2.5).\n2. **Databricks \u2014 Solutions Architect \u2013 Strategic High Tech** (posted ~1 day ago, Remote-CA, **$180k\u2013$247.5k**) \u2014 7/10. His exact current title + GCP/Python/PyTorch; gaps: tenure, CA region, SQL, travel willingness.\n3. **Baseten \u2014 Forward Deployed Engineer (Training)** (reposted today) \u2014 6/10 backup; RL/SFT is a hard requirement, which is a genuine gap.\n\n**Fellowships (paid, you work for the org \u2014 funding-only grants excluded):**\n1. **Anthropic Fellows Program \u2014 Jan 2027 cohort** (rolling, $3,850/wk + ~$15k/mo compute, no PhD required) \u2014 8.5/10, best of the day; the ML Systems workstream maps to his Vertex AI + agentic ETL experience.\n2. **Baseten Base Labs Fellowship** (rolling, ~$15k + housing/compute, SF, starts late Sept 2026) \u2014 5.5/10; PhD/publication criteria are real gaps, kept as honorable mention, no drafts.\n\nExcluded with reasons: OpenAI Residency (closed), Apple AIML Residency (no fresh opening), July-2026 Anthropic cohort (closed Apr 26), and unverified aggregator listings.\n\n**Drafts for the top 3** (cover letters + resume tweaks, all grounded in resume.txt wi