INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-323e6f76c9','task-db9b445c7a',1787556621.28488349,'{"task_id": "task-db9b445c7a", "run_id": "run-323e6f76c9", "started_at": 1787556621.2848835, "finished_at": 1787557542.1181755, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Done. Here''s what the evidence actually showed and what I wrote.\n\n**Key finding vs. last week''s file:** big state change \u2014 openEvolve moved from \"Phase 2 in flight\" to **Phase 3 active**. Phase 2 is fully closed (4/4 items, 71 tests, per `PHASE2.md`), and you''ve been grinding Phase 3 all of 08-22\u219224 (five builder sessions of 231/322/367/274/54 messages). The \"what replaces the surrogate-offline docking proxy\" open question is **resolved** \u2014 the Vina adapter shipped (`2529fa0`) and, per the brain thread, the SMILES\u2192PDBQT seam (`6f71a30`) closed too. What''s genuinely stuck now: **live-docking can''t run on this host** \u2014 no vina binary, no meeko/OpenBabel \u2014 so the fake-vina harness is the only proof of the real path.\n\n**Active (5, ranked by evidence):** openEvolve/Phase 3 \u2192 OpenWorker app itself (20+ commits 08-22/23 on MCP-tool grants + honest run-stop markers) \u2192 job/grant pipeline (unchanged open question: 37 drafts, *nothing sent*) \u2192 workstation-stack (edge of window, last commit 08-21) \u2192 research corpus (standing watch, 2 papers this week).\n\n**Quiet:** dcode-stack (last 2026-08-16, 8 days untouched) and the Sigma market brief (disabled since 08-15) \u2014 carried over, not deleted. **Parked:** left verbatim (empty, as was).\n\n**Distribution:** copied to canonical `OpenWorker/knowledge/FOCUS.md` + all **149** task workspaces, verified `149/149` \u2014 matches the workspace count exactly, no shortfall. llama.cpp and LibreChat explicitly excluded as upstream clones (authorship: Gerganov/Avila, not you).\n\nReport file: `FOCUS.md` in both your scratch workspace and `~/OpenWorker/knowledge/`.", "artifacts": ["FOCUS.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-323e6f76c9"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-2af5f70b0e','task-1b2c4d3f13',1787558421.30931448,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-2af5f70b0e", "started_at": 1787558421.3093145, "finished_at": 1787561672.3130722, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Done \u2014 `papers-2026-08-24.md` is written to the task workspace.\n\nThe digest covers the **2608.213xx batch (posted 2026-08-21, new to this record since the 08-23 run) plus three honest catch-ups** (Pratt Symposium, Dral Perspective, Faraday''s companion), none of which appeared in any prior output. The three ON-FOCUS items all sit in the scoring/verification layer FOCUS.md is working on right now for OpenEvolve Phase 3:\n\n- **Quantum** \u2014 Davoudi & Stryker: ~10\u00b9\u2074\u00d7 param-independent cost cut in QCD product-formula simulation via a *fixable* inefficiency in the existing bound (audit the cost estimate, not just the algorithm).\n- **ML** \u2014 Yang et al.: the first stage-wise size-scaling study of self-refinement \u2014 refiner and generator reward size, critic barely does, an *undersized refiner actively hurts*. Most actionable line this run: the judgment/execution split for a local-27B fleet is asymmetric, not uniform.\n- **RSI** \u2014 Granqvist/AstraZeneca: deployed LLM-judge with 5-annotator human alignment (0.80\u21920.86) and deterministic tool-call checks \u2014 the constructive counterpart to Phantom Gains. Plus Pratt''s Symposium (agent-independent immutable record layer) \u2014 fits the Claude-Science-class provenance goal in memory #6.\n\nCross-topic finding: all three ON-FOCUS items are the same question \u2014 \"how do you know your scoring layer is right\" \u2014 seen from three angles. Eureka''s math claim is still unverified (6th consecutive run).", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-08-24.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-2af5f70b0e"}');
