INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-8369741baa','task-78fcb8b740',1787737503.20044112,'{"task_id": "task-78fcb8b740", "run_id": "run-8369741baa", "started_at": 1787737503.2004411, "finished_at": 1787742268.3224103, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Target: the OpenEvolve drug front''s approach \u2014 LLM free-mutating SMILES strings, steered by a budget ledger over a tiered ladder whose workhorse signal is the Vina docking score (Phase 3 closed 08-25; this attacks what Phase 4 runs on). The core finding is that the approach splits into three separable parts, and the weakest is **the operator, not the loop**: ToolMol (arXiv:2605.12784) shows tool-backed RDKit editing beats LLM direct-mutation even after fixing validity, your own Phase 2 history shows the SMILES mutator collapsing diversity to clones, and the scoring signal it feeds carries real risk (Vina R\u00b2 ~0.25\u20130.5, worse on flexible ligands and GPCRs). So: abandon free-form LLM SMILES mutation in favor of a fixed tool set, and borrow cost-cooled allocation (CArBO) from AutoML since your budget ledger already computes every input it needs. Falsification test is a one-hour A/B: deterministic RDKit operators vs the LLM operator, compared on validity, duplicate rate, and top-5 rank at equal budget. Written to **outside-view-2026-08-26.md** (6 searches, 8 page reads, within budget).", "artifacts": ["outside-view-2026-08-26.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-8369741baa"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-53466dafa2','task-ecad448aa3',1787738403.22384905,'{"task_id": "task-ecad448aa3", "run_id": "run-53466dafa2", "started_at": 1787738403.223849, "finished_at": 1787749646.0119638, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Done \u2014 full run complete.\n\n**25 new findings stored** (5 jobs, 2 news, 7 breakage, 11 papers) from the four automation outputs modified since yesterday; **8 candidates skipped** as already-stored dups (Horizon deadline, ROCR #7051 and #6634 \u2014 explicitly carried, not re-reported) or unchanged carryovers (Claude Corps, OpenAI Residency, Quantum Circuits).\n\nState changes called out explicitly: Iran''s \"Operation Economic Outcast\" **landed** Aug 25 (was \"scheduled presser\" Aug 22\u201324); **Ollama v0.33.0 final is out** (was \"rc3, hold off\" \u2014 upgrade to the broken-Linux-packaging fix is now safe); **OpenWorker upstream is v0.2.1** with an \"updating is recommended\" security line that maps directly onto your unattended-fleet question; the Strix-Halo unsloth SIGSEGV workaround got its first verified full read (404''d last week).\n\nCaveats, recorded in the ledger: the `mcp__qdrant__qdrant-find` bridge was flaky all run (~6 of 14 calls errored) while store and HTTP stayed healthy, so dedup for a few items leaned on the 08-24 ledger''s stored list \u2014 safe by construction since both jobs log every point. Running total verified live: **KB at 58 points** (33 before this run).\n\nLedger: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge/ingest/2026-08-26.md` (working copy in the scratch workspace). Brain threads updated: job-search (Horizon due Aug 30; still drafts-only), local-stack-breakage, workstation-stack, automation-fleet.", "artifacts": ["ledger-2026-08-26.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-53466dafa2"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-4e7e1cc808','task-1b2c4d3f13',1787817615.17139768,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-4e7e1cc808", "started_at": 1787817615.1713977, "finished_at": 1787818119.428812, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. The 2026-08-27 run found 8 genuinely-new papers since the 08-26 run (everything submitted 08-25/08-26).\n\n**What I found:**\n- **ON-FOCUS quantum (2):** Distributed Trotterization with *optimal time-scaling entanglement cost* \u2014 the product-formula cost result the Phase-3 audit line (Davoudi\u2013Stryker) wanted, with a matching lower bound (2608.25896); Certified decoding of qLDPC codes \u2014 an auditable QEC decoder that attaches an optimality certificate to each decision (2608.25545).\n- **ON-FOCUS ML (2):** TailSFT \u2014 filtering already-fit sequences during SFT makes the *checkpoint* RL-ready (up to 17% pass@16 gain, 4% further at GRPO) (2608.25756); Reflection Steering \u2014 a training-free way to cut reasoning-token waste by orthogonalizing reflection from reasoning (16.9% tokens saved) (2608.25542).\n- **ON-FOCUS RSI (3):** FrontierChallenge \u2014 75.5% of non-passing Claude Code trajectories still *claimed* completion (strongest new evidence for the Phantom Gains warning); KOPE \u2014 Experience-Graph memory with a fixed model (pass 55\u219285%) \u2014 second independent confirmation of the \"harness, not model, is the lever\" thesis; SwarmWorld \u2014 stigmergic tech-evolution societies.\n- **ADJACENT (1):** LoRA rank-error bounds for attention (2608.26052).\n\n**Tooling note:** the arXiv MCP tools aren''t in this session''s toolset, so I ran the run on the live arXiv \"recent\" listings + individual `abs` pages (all read in full). A heads-up: the `sortBy=submissionDate` and `submittedDate:` operators on the arXiv API return 400/500 in this environment \u2014 the listing pages worked fine, so no issue.\n\nThe artifact is written: **`/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-1b2c4d3f13/papers-2026-08-27.md`**, and I carried the FrontierChallenge anchor forward into the running-record thread.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-08-27.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-4e7e1cc808"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-57c4521a7f','task-f471043f3e',1787818515.17894554,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-57c4521a7f", "started_at": 1787818515.1789455, "finished_at": 1787818775.5101995, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote **`breakage-2026-08-27.md`**.\n\n**What I found:** One net-new release since 2026-08-26, and it''s not a new break vector \u2014 **ollama v0.33.1** is a 3-commit MLX/Metal housekeeping release; the ROCm Linux wheel is still in it, and the only family-touching item (`cmake: make external compat patches idempotent`) is a build-time hardening commit, unverified on the CMake-4.x axis. **transformers latest moved v5.15.1 \u2192 v5.16.1**, but your 5.5.0 sits below it on the same 5.x line and 5.16.1''s changes are addbacks, not breakers \u2014 so that''s a carry-forward, not a finding. Everything else is unchanged: OpenWorker v0.2.1, llama.cpp v0.3.0/b10621, unsloth v0.1.803-beta, and the top gfx1151 runtime risk (TheRock #7051 and #6634, both open, zero movement).\n\n**Important honesty note:** both network search tools were *down* this run \u2014 Tavily returned `getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN` and Exa returned `fetch failed` on every attempt, so I ran **0 net-new searches**. I did not reconstruct any regression news from memory. All the items I *did* report (the version bumps and their release notes) were verified directly via the GitHub REST API and by opening the release pages \u2014 those stand. The gfx1151/ROCm/torch-wheel standing items are reported as \"unchanged from 08-26, unexpanded\" rather than \"confirmed clean.\" Worth retrying a search pass when the tools recover if you want the gfx1151 surface actually refreshed.", "artifacts": ["breakage-2026-08-27.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-57c4521a7f"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-8471f51c62','task-c6cf366b90',1787819715.19008207,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-8471f51c62", "started_at": 1787819715.190082, "finished_at": 1787820326.300443, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. This run produced the 2026-08-27 brief plus three new draft pairs.\n\n**What I found:** The day''s standout is **Humana''s Senior AI Software Engineer** \u2014 genuinely fresh (posted ~4h ago, ~$107k\u2013147k, US-remote with Tampa/Fort Lauderdale as designated locations), and unusually close to the resume: insurance-document RAG + SLM-agent ETL from Mutual of Omaha + end-to-end GCP Vertex ownership from Hewani map almost 1:1 onto its stack (RAG, LLM orchestration, Python/TS, evals, vector DBs, HIPAA). Also a strong new match on **LangChain''s AI Engineer, Enablement** (LangChain is literally named on your resume) and a new top **fellowship \u2014 the Applied Data Fellowship at Harris/University of Chicago**, whose best fit-point is that it''s essentially a mirror of the ADI Fellowship you already hold. I re-verified the time-critical **Horizon 2027 deadline is still open \u2014 Aug 30 (3 days left)**; OpenAI Residency and the Anthropic Fellows Program remain closed.\n\nFiles written:\n- **`jobs-2026-08-27.md`** \u2014 the ranked shortlist with ON-FOCUS / ADJACENT tags, continuity vs. 2026-08-26, and full fit/gap assessments\n- `drafts/cover-letter-Humana.md` + `drafts/resume-tweaks-Humana.md`\n- `drafts/cover-letter-ADF.md` + `drafts/resume-tweaks-ADF.md`\n- `drafts/cover-letter-LangChain.md` + `drafts/resume-tweaks-LangChain.md`\n\nAll drafts are evidence-based and flag the honest gaps (no degree; ~2yr production timeline) without inventing anything. No applications were submitted, per spec.", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-08-27.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-LangChain.md", "drafts/cover-letter-Humana.md", "drafts/cover-letter-LangChain.md", "drafts/cover-letter-ADF.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-ADF.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-Humana.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-8471f51c62"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-3092df9ccb','task-c685e22a0b',1787822415.20915627,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-3092df9ccb", "started_at": 1787822415.2091563, "finished_at": 1787822560.5940204, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone \u2014 written to `morning-briefing-2026-08-27.md` in the workspace.\n\nWhat actually moved in the last 24h: the AI model-tap, dry since Aug 22, drip-ed **two fresh frontier \"Flash\" models on Aug 26** \u2014 **GLM-5.3-Flash** from Z.ai and **Qwen3.8-Flash-Next** from Qwen (verified on the release tracker I opened, but I found no usable benchmark/context details \u2014 I withheld specs rather than invent them). The other genuinely new item is **Trump''s Aug 26 emergency over foreign-made electric-grid equipment**. I also carried forward verifiable continuity: **India\u2013China''s \"early and substantial harvest\" border outcome** (Aug 26, confirmed on The Hindu), and the **Iran sanctions** (Pezeshkian dismissed them Aug 26) now in aftershock, not escalation. Local inference / ROCm is quiet, so I left it as a carried-forward Ollama 0.33.0-rc3 note.\n\nBudget: 4 searches, 3 fetches. Two tools were down early (Tavily DNS failure, Exa fetch failure) so I ran on `web_search`/`web_fetch` via DuckDuckGo \u2014 all cited claims are from pages I actually opened, and I flagged the one detail (GLM benchmarks) I could not verify.", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-08-27.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-3092df9ccb"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-a1a8e559b5','task-ecad448aa3',1787824815.23539376,'{"task_id": "task-ecad448aa3", "run_id": "run-a1a8e559b5", "started_at": 1787824815.2353938, "finished_at": 1787828350.21338, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. The KB ingest for 2026-08-27 ran: I found 8 new findings (5 papers, 2 breakage, 1 news), deduped them via Qdrant `/points/query`, and stored all 8 \u2014 confirmed live.\n\n**But a serious incident came up:** the knowledge base''s `default` collection was at **0 points** when I started this run and is now 8. The 50 points recorded on 2026-08-26 and 2026-08-24 (ledgers claim 58, then 34) are gone, and recreating the collection didn''t restore them. This is data loss \u2014 likely a Qdrant reset/non-persistence between 08-26 and now, not my recreate. The 08-26 `papers` and `breakage` files are still on disk, so those points could be restored verbatim without fabrication; the 08-26 `jobs`/`morning-briefing` files weren''t opened this run, so they can''t be restored verbatim.\n\nThis is a decision for you (the ledger lists concrete next steps). I flagged it in the ledger and recorded it in the automation-fleet thread so a future session doesn''t still report \"58 points.\"\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Ledger: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge/ingest/2026-08-27.md`\n- Report: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/__task__task-ecad448aa3/report.md`\n- Raw run data: `ingest_kb.json`; ingest script: `ingest_kb.py`", "artifacts": ["report.md", "ingest_kb.py", "ingest_kb.json"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-a1a8e559b5"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-8a021c83f9','task-1b2c4d3f13',1787904015.98043227,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-8a021c83f9", "started_at": 1787904015.9804323, "finished_at": 1787904325.9903197, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. This run''s `papers-2026-08-28.md` is written to the workspace.\n\n**What I found:** Window was papers submitted 2026-08-27 (all new relative to 08-27''s 2608.26081 top-out). Rather than re-deriving, I carried forward the 08-27 record and the FOCUS.md state \u2014 the FrontierChallenge gap and Phase-3 cost question are unchanged, so I spent the budget on genuinely new work.\n\n- **Quantum (\u00a71):** *Find Rows and Columns and Decode* (arXiv:2608.27211) \u2014 linear-time, logarithmic-depth expander-code decoder; a concrete *decode-cost* result bearing on the OpenEvolve Phase-3 QM-tier question.\n- **ML (\u00a72):** *Understanding ES for LLM Reasoning* (2608.27351) \u2014 ES beats GRPO via broader coverage + sparse, forgetting-free updates at lower memory budget, directly actionable for the constrained fleet. *Circuit Condensation* (2608.27254) \u2014 post-training shrinks mechanistic circuits ~8\u00d7 average (up to 316\u00d7); weight updates, not search, drive the reduction.\n- **RSI (\u00a73, strongest cluster):** *AgentFold* (2608.26747) \u2014 closed-loop agentic search over a 2,000+ line folding codebase, +7.5% over Codex, and the prior \"soft priors + gated refinement beat geometric perturbation\" is a real, testable design rule. *HarnessLens* (2608.27311) \u2014 behavior-aware harness evolution (+7.6\u201313.6%, model-weight-free) \u2014 two independent confirmations of the record''s \"structure-around-the-model is the load-bearing lever\" prior.\n\nThe cross-topic read: the gain lives in the structure (memory, harness, decoder, update mechanism), not the model \u2014 and today''s RSI picks add a \"when does a self-improvement step stick\" prior, not just another \"structure matters\" statement.\n\nNote: same environment constraint as 08-27 \u2014 the MCP arXiv tools weren''t in my toolset this run, so I read the live arXiv listings/abs pages directly rather than the MCP tools, per the \"web over shell\" instruction. No shell was used.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-08-28.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-8a021c83f9"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-b2f1259732','task-f471043f3e',1787904915.99053788,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-b2f1259732", "started_at": 1787904915.990538, "finished_at": 1787905098.9236012, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nRun complete. **`breakage-2026-08-28.md`** is written.\n\n**What I found:** One net-new release since 08-27 \u2014 **unsloth v0.1.804-beta** (2026-08-27 13:09 UTC, \"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next + GLM-5.3-Flash\"). It''s an additive model-adapter beta with no visible gfx1151/AMD break, but because unsloth is the package historically responsible for the wrong-torch CUDA-substitution trap on this box, the practical read is the standing guardrail: any fresh `pip install -U unsloth` here re-triggers re-installing torch from the gfx1151 index + `BNB_ROCM_VERSION=71` / `UNSLOTH_MOE_BACKEND=native_torch`. Everything else confirmed unchanged via direct GitHub API \u2014 TheRock #7051 (top gfx1151 runtime risk) re-opened in full, still open/triage, zero movement; ollama v0.33.1, transformers v5.16.1, llama.cpp v0.3.0, OpenWorker v0.2.1.\n\n**Caveat, stated plainly:** Tavily''s search backend was down again this run (`getaddrinfo EAI_AGAIN` \u2014 3rd consecutive run: 08-26/27/28), so **0 of 6 searches were used** and no new ROCm/graphics-stack regression could be *discovered*. The standing gfx1151/ROCm/CMake-4.x/spirv-headers items are reported as \"unchanged from 08-27, unexpanded,\" not \"confirmed clean.\" All version-of-record and issue-state values came from direct GitHub REST API + release/issue-page opens, not from memory. I flagged this recurring search-outage as a durable condition in the record so cold future runs don''t try to reconstruct release notes from memory.", "artifacts": ["breakage-2026-08-28.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-b2f1259732"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-8b545b768c','task-c6cf366b90',1787906115.99959301,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-8b545b768c", "started_at": 1787906115.999593, "finished_at": 1787906835.5476527, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. The 2026-08-28 shortlist is written to `jobs-2026-08-28.md` in the workspace, with tailored draft sets for the top 3 matches.\n\n**What I found:** Day quality was moderate-to-strong. Beyond tracking the carryover items (Horizon 2027 still open \u2014 ~2 days to its Aug 30 deadline; OpenAI residency couldn''t be re-verified today \u2014 returned 403 \u2014 carried as \"closed, last verified 08-26\"; Claude Corps still future), I found:\n\n- **UnitedHealthcare \u2014 Senior AI/ML Engineer** (new, posted ~4 days ago): today''s strongest match \u2014 healthcare-domain RAG + LLM + NLP + underwriting/insurance + vector DB + MLOps, mapped 1:1 onto the Mutual of Omaha RAG + SLM-agent work and Hewani GCP Vertex ownership, with the degree screen waived by \"equivalent experience.\" **Apply \u2014 top priority.**\n- **Laurel \u2014 Applied AI Engineer** (remote, ~8-day fresh, $254k\u2013$328k comp range): strong LLM-app + evaluation + Python/TS fit, but the **7-yr SE bar makes it a genuine reach** (degree is waivable).\n- **CHEQ \u2014 AI Engineer** (fresh): a nearly 1:1 **GCP-first + LangChain + RAG + embeddings** stack match, but almost certainly **in-office (Tel Aviv/Bengaluru)** \u2014 flagged as a reach until remote is confirmed.\n\n**Fellowships:** The standout finding is the **Horizon \"AI for Science\" Fellowship** (DOE national labs, frontier AI, $200k, no clearance) \u2014 arguably the single best-matching fellowship on the map (quantum/QM-ML adjacency + the OpenEvolve Phase 3 chemistry stack + 2+-yr-ML bar) \u2014 but its **2026 cycle already closed July 31**. Watched and recorded so it isn''t lost to the next cycle. Also new: **Cambridge ERA:AI Fellowship** (AI safety research, \u00a310k stipend, deadline **Sep 13**).\n\nDrafts written for all three (cover letter + resume tweaks each). Note one honest caveat: CHEQ is remote-unconfirmed and should not be applied to unless a US/remote location is verified, and Laurel is a tenure-reach \u2014 both caveats are spelled out in their files. No applications were sent.", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-08-28.md", "drafts/cover-letter-UnitedHealthcare.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-UnitedHealthcare.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-CHEQ.md", "drafts/cover-letter-CHEQ.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-Laurel.md", "drafts/cover-letter-Laurel.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-8b545b768c"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-3929728561','task-c685e22a0b',1787908816.02711319,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-3929728561", "started_at": 1787908816.0271132, "finished_at": 1787909045.9026008, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nBriefing is written. The day genuinely moved, but not the way the last two had: the OpenAI/o3 retirement and the two Chinese open drops are now settled context, while the fresh catalysts were a local-inference release and a compute-chip-driven market rally.\n\nThe one clear state change vs. yesterday''s brief is **Ollama 0.33.1 shipping** (Aug 26) \u2014 the final I''d flagged as \"imminent\" is out, which means your pinned LibreChat ollama is no longer on a prerelease, plus 0.33.2-rc0 landed Aug 27. The other real news: **Nvidia''s Wed earnings beat** drove a Thursday rebound (S&P +0.72% to 7,731, Nasdaq +1.57%) with the Fed''s next-move risk still on the table, and a **fresh China-trade escalation** (US weighing a 7.5% tariff over \"overcapacity,\" Beijing threatening countermeasures). ROCm itself was quiet \u2014 no 24h drop, ROCm 10.0.0 is still the freshest doc and 7.2.2 your Strix Halo baseline. The Iran thread continues but hasn''t escalated (Netanyahu ruling out diplomacy).\n\n**File:** `morning-briefing-2026-08-28.md` \u2014 5 bullets, budget exactly 5 searches / 4 fetches. All figures were read directly from the pages I opened (releasebot, Rio Times economy briefing, Livemint live blog); ROCm details are search-result only, flagged as such, and I skipped stale 2025 Russia-summit noise rather than cite it.", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-08-28.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-3929728561"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-ea9ff7eeb4','task-ecad448aa3',1787911216.05047273,'{"task_id": "task-ecad448aa3", "run_id": "run-ea9ff7eeb4", "started_at": 1787911216.0504727, "finished_at": 1787912642.6251771, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Ran the scheduled KB ingest against the 5 automation outputs from 2026-08-28.\n\n**Result: 13 new findings stored, KB now at 21 points** (was 8 after the 08-27 run). No duplicates, nothing left behind.\n\nON-FOCUS (8): 5 papers \u2014 AgentFold & HarnessLens confirming \"structure around the model is the load-bearing lever\" (RSI cluster, directly on-topic for OpenEvolve''s self-improving loop), ES beats GRPO, Circuit Condensation, and OSTRE quantum-expander-code decode-cost floor \u2014 plus unsloth v0.1.804-beta (first unsloth release stored this job), and job matches UnitedHealthcare/Laurel/CHEQ and Horizon AI-for-Science. ADJACENT (3): LLMs-as-OR-algorithm-designers, the 7.5% China tariff, and Cambridge ERA:AI reopening.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n- **Dedup got me the first time.** The mandated cosine-0.72 find-first reported 10 \"duplicates,\" but they were false positives \u2014 each top-matched a *different* stored point on a tiny 8-point collection. None shared an identifier, so I re-ran with identifier-aware dedup and stored all 10. Lesson recorded in the ledger: **identifier match, not cosine, is the reliable dup test** when the collection is small.\n- **Horizon 2027 Fellowship closes 2026-08-30** \u2014 ~1 day out, still drafts-only, zero applications sent. Time-critical, carried forward.\n\nThe 08-24/08-26 data-loss (50 points) remains unrecovered, and the GitHub MCP gateway is now unreachable (fetch failed, 3rd consecutive run) instead of the earlier bad-token error.\n\nReport: `/home/iconbaypark2900/openworker-tasks/__task__task-ecad448aa3/report.md` \u2014 ledger at `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge/ingest/2026-08-28.md`. Updated threads: automation-fleet, breakage watch, job-search, workstation-stack, paper-watch.", "artifacts": ["ledger-2026-08-28.md", "report.md", "ingest_kb_2026-08-28.json", "ingest_kb_2026-08-28.py", "ingest_kb_append_2026-08-28.py"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-ea9ff7eeb4"}');
