INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-d179b3b605','task-db9b445c7a',1788161427.16253137,'{"task_id": "task-db9b445c7a", "run_id": "run-d179b3b605", "started_at": 1788161427.1625314, "finished_at": 1788161639.3361056, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. FOCUS.md is written to the knowledge root, staged to my workspace, and distributed to all 169 `__task__` workspaces.\n\nThis run''s FOCUS.md (2026-08-31) shows the live build has moved: **agpack** (8 sessions, 189\u2013330 msgs each on 08-30, top open question \"P0 unblock deployment/ship it\") has overtaken the stage, **dcode-stack** came back from quiet with 51 commits on its vLLM/llama.cpp proxy, and **openworker** (40 commits to 08-30) still carries the unattended-fleet question. **openEvolve''s repo is gone** off disk \u2014 only knowledge threads remain \u2014 so its Phase 3 work is parked. **workstation-stack** revived to a 08-29 commit (LibreChat secrets backup). Job pipeline unchanged \u2014 still drafts, no sent applications. Distributed 169/169.\n\nFile: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/knowledge/FOCUS.md` (also at `openworker-tasks/__task__task-db9b445c7a/FOCUS.md`).", "artifacts": ["FOCUS.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-d179b3b605"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-c6516272e4','task-1b2c4d3f13',1788163227.18253302,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-c6516272e4", "started_at": 1788163227.182533, "finished_at": 1788163790.7219515, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote `papers-2026-08-31.md` to the workspace.\n\n**What I found (submitted 2026-08-28 \u2014 the freshest arXiv had indexed at read time; 08-29/08-30 haven''t entered the new-submission cycle yet):**\n\n- **Quantum (ON-FOCUS):** A neural message-passing *decoder* for concatenated stabilizer codes that roughly **doubles the depolarizing pseudo-threshold (6.5%\u219212.3%)** on the $[[15,7,3]]$ code ([2608.28571](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28571)). New decoder-threshold number for the OpenEvolve Phase-3 QM-budget question, not a new fault-tolerant threshold.\n- **ML (ON-FOCUS):** A **size-weight frontier** that makes synthetic-augmented inference coverage-guaranteed by *calibrated weighting* instead of piling on synthetic data ([2608.28576](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28576)).\n- **RSI (ON-FOCUS):** \"Certified Code World Models\" \u2014 proves an agent''s model of its own tools can be *exactly right on everything the harness can reach and arbitrary beyond it*, formalized as a **gate-quotient** where \"reach is gauge,\" with a \"danger is topology relative to reach\" principle ([2608.28541](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28541)). A strong new formal anchor for the record''s Phantom Gains / trust thread.\n- **ADJACENT:** A systematic review concluding security agents \"can act but **not** have bounded authority or auditable behavior\" ([2608.28490](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28490)); plus sliding-window attention beating post-trained linear attention ([2608.28444](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.28444)). Cap of 3 ADJACENT used.\n\n**Continuity:** Astar and WikiSkill (both 08-27) were already reported 08-28, so not re-stated. The running theme held: the gain and the cheat both live in the boundary between what a system can do and what it''s measured on \u2014 decoder threshold, calibrated weighting, and reachable-set topology state it in three languages.\n\nOne honest note: the arXiv MCP tools weren''t connected to this session (this persona''s gateway only carries the tavily/exa/context7/web stack per my memory), so I sourced through the **arXiv Atom API via the `web_fetch` tool** \u2014 the permitted web fallback, never shell/curl. Every abstract was read in full before citation, and I flagged where only pseudo-thresholds/empirical claims were claimed rather than proven thresholds.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-08-31.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-c6516272e4"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-32d9743178','task-f471043f3e',1788164127.19963884,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-32d9743178", "started_at": 1788164127.1996388, "finished_at": 1788164422.0573447, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nThe breakage-2026-08-31.md file is correctly in place. The run is complete:\n\n- **Net-new release:** ollama moved 0.33.1 \u2192 **v0.33.2** (2026-08-27 20:31) \u2014 macOS-app / Claude-Desktop-proxy housekeeping; **no Linux/ROCm change**, not a break vector for your box.\n- **Net-new corroborate:** legacy-rocm-build **#6522** \u2014 second independent open report of the gfx1151 AsyncEventsLoop 100%-CPU spin (same class as TheRock #7051). Both are open, AMD-triage, zero movement. The gfx1151 top runtime risk now has two open reports instead of one.\n- **Unchanged vs 08-28:** transformers v5.16.1, llama.cpp v0.3.0/b10621, OpenWorker v0.2.1, unsloth v0.1.804-beta \u2014 your 5.5.0/7.13.0 are unaffected by their latest addbacks.\n- **Budget:** Tavily `EAI_AGAIN` (5th consecutive run) + MCP context7 now also failing (`TypeError: fetch failed`). All priority checks ran via DuckDuckGo `web_search` + direct GitHub REST API; nothing reconstructed from memory.\n\nWrote `breakage-2026-08-31.md` and recorded both durable findings to the dependency-breakage and local-stack-breakage threads.", "artifacts": ["breakage-2026-08-31.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-32d9743178"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-00d93e0b99','task-c6cf366b90',1788165327.21300959,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-00d93e0b99", "started_at": 1788165327.2130096, "finished_at": 1788165579.333829, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. This run''s key finding: **Horizon 2027 has closed.**\n\nThe day was thin by design \u2014 I kept it honest rather than padding it. The only genuinely new, live, actionable target is the **MATS Residency Winter 2027**, an in-person AI-safety residency (Berkeley/London, 12 weeks, ~$6.4k/mo + up to $16k/mo compute) that explicitly requires **no PhD** \u2014 a match for your self-taught, ships-for-real profile. Its deadline is **October 31, 2026**, and I drafted both files for it.\n\nThe honest gate on MATS isn''t skills \u2014 it''s logistics: a 12-week physical presence for a US-based applicant.\n\nOne important state change, carried from the prior three runs: **the Horizon 2027 Fellowship deadline (Aug 30) has passed** \u2014 I re-verified the program page still says \"Apply by August 30, 2026,\" and today is the 31st. The drafts were carried 08-26\u219227\u219228 but never submitted, so this cycle is lost; the program is annual, so watch for the 2028 cohort in summer 2027.\n\nThe strong standard-role matches from 08-28 (UnitedHealthcare, Laurel, CHEQ) are unchanged carryover \u2014 drafts already in `drafts/`, no fresh posting surfaced.\n\nFiles written to this workspace:\n- **`jobs-2026-08-31.md`** \u2014 the dated shortlist (ON-FOCUS MATS fellowship, ADJACENT carryover + exclusions)\n- **`drafts/cover-letter-MATS.md`**\n- **`drafts/resume-tweaks-MATS.md`**", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-08-31.md", "drafts/cover-letter-MATS.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-MATS.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-00d93e0b99"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-d76f801758','task-c685e22a0b',1788168027.2423861,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-d76f801758", "started_at": 1788168027.242386, "finished_at": 1788168181.0297368, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDelivered. Here''s what I found and why it''s thin on the AI side:\n\nThe AI/ML industry and your local-inference stack were **quiet in the last 24h** \u2014 the freshest tracked release is Tencent''s \"Hy4 preview\" (Aug 28), and nothing new came from OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta, or xAI, so the AI-industry layer is genuinely thin and the dcode-stack/Strix Halo box has no new dated version to adopt. What *actually* moved was in world news: **(1)** a Nepal glacier collapse triggered flood disasters nearing **800 dead** with **85 US citizens missing** in Nepal/Tibet; **(2)** a new US financial action against Egypt''s Banque Misr over Iran links (de-escalated, not escalated, via a joint UAE/Egypt statement) \u2014 threading into the Iran sanctions run carried since Aug 25; and **(3)** a fuel-macro shift \u2014 India now shipping ~1M barrels of gasoline to Russia. All are tagged ADJACENT; FOCUS (agpack/dcode-stack/openEvolve) had no external move today, which I said plainly rather than inventing one.\n\nFile: **morning-briefing-2026-08-31.md**\n\nBudget used: 5 searches, 4 fetches. Note: AI Herald''s \"news today\" page was stale (top story dated Jul 12) and the geopolitics substack 403''d, so neither is cited.", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-08-31.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-d76f801758"}');
