INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-931c3f3e93','task-fe38324f51',1788305882.66348886,'{"task_id": "task-fe38324f51", "run_id": "run-931c3f3e93", "started_at": 1788305882.6634889, "finished_at": 1788306177.821157, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nThe run is complete. Here''s the summary.\n\n## This run (third apply drive, 2026-09-01)\n\n**One application inspected and triaged** \u2014 **Further \u2014 Senior AI Engineer** (Greenhouse, `job-boards.greenhouse.io/further/jobs/8406645002`).\n\n- **Valtech was the top target but is already closed + logged**, so by rule 2 the highest-ranked ON-FOCUS target not yet in the ledger was **Further**, which has a full draft.\n- I drove the live Greenhouse form and applied the hard triage rule: **15 required fields / 7 combobox dropdowns** \u2014 far over the 8-fields / 2-dropdown auto-fill threshold. So I **did not** attempt a 40-minute long-form fill that would have burned the whole run. Instead I recorded a **`manual` handoff** \u2014 which the spec counts as a success.\n- Every required field is answerable from `facts.md`, so I wrote the exact field-by-field answers (name, email, phone, US/No sponsorship, `$100k+, negotiable`, \"Less than 4 years\", relocation Yes, near-office **No** \u2014 Fort Lauderdale isn''t within commuting distance of their offices). The one real gap is the cover-letter box accepts an *upload*, but the draft is markdown-only, so you''d need to paste or convert it.\n\n**Recorded** (both places, matching how the morning and PM runs each appended):\n- **Ledger row** \u2014 `2026-09-01 | Further (via Miragely) | Senior AI Engineer | targets.md | manual | \u2026` with the direct URL, field/dropdown counts, the question labels not answerable from facts.md, and the full answer map.\n- **applied-2026-09-01.md** \u2014 a new \"3-run 2026-09-01\" section with form details, the field-by-field answers, and a \"needs an answer from me\" block.\n\n**Next in the queue:** **Bybit (Recommendation ML Engineer)** \u2014 next ranked ON-FOCUS pick with a full draft set, ready for the next `apply` run.\n\nNo auto-submit happened this run, but the record is intact and the queue advanced cleanly \u2014 the only real failure here would have been writing nothing.\n\n[Applied record \u2014 2026-09-01](applied-2026-09-01.md) \u00b7 [Ledger](ledger.md)", "artifacts": ["ledger.md", "applied-2026-09-01.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-931c3f3e93"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-4763542dd1','task-c6cf366b90',1788306332.66820216,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-4763542dd1", "started_at": 1788306332.6682022, "finished_at": 1788307057.9230654, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone \u2014 final run on 2026-09-01 complete.\n\n**What I found:** I carried the three prior runs forward (didn''t overwrite them) and the new finding of this run is a strong, 1:1-posture match: **Google Cloud \u2014 Forward Deployed Engineer (Generative AI) III**, $174k\u2013$252k + 15% bonus + equity, US locations with preferred-location option. The job description is essentially a restatement of the applicant''s current Hewani work \u2014 full-lifecycle Vertex AI, RAG, SLM-agent ETL, evaluation/observability \u2014 so I drafted a tailored cover letter plus resume-tweaks, leading with full-lifecycle AI ownership (the honest gate is the 5-yr software bar, not the shape of the work).\n\nFor the seven already-drafted programmes, the only thing new this run was the **deadline check** (which had never been done): **MATS Residency is OPEN until Oct 31 2026 AoE** (top priority to apply), **ADF, CTEC, CSC Generation, and Lila are OPEN** (apply early; Lila has a degree bar he lacks), and **GovAI and AIAF are CLOSED** for the 2026 cycle.\n\nFiles: **`jobs-2026-09-01-PM3.md`** (final shortlist; morning/PM outputs preserved), **`drafts/cover-letter-googlecloud-fde.md`**, and **`drafts/resume-tweaks-googlecloud-fde.md`** \u2014 all drafts only, no applications submitted.", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-09-01-PM3.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-googlecloud-fde.md", "drafts/cover-letter-googlecloud-fde.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-4763542dd1"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-718bba4e0d','task-9b2a9d143b',1788309872.70166397,'{"task_id": "task-9b2a9d143b", "run_id": "run-718bba4e0d", "started_at": 1788309872.701664, "finished_at": 1788310256.5917783, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. `revenue-2026-09-01.md` is written and it was my final action, as required.\n\n## What I produced\n\n**Continuity:** Cold start \u2014 no prior `revenue-*.md` and **no FOCUS.md** existed in the workspace, so I tagged findings manually and flagged that FOCUS.md was missing (the next run, if it exists elsewhere, should re-tag with it).\n\n**6 ranked findings, ranked by EV per hour of your time:**\n\n1. **huntr \"Inside Job\" \u2014 $15,000 pot, ends Sept 14** (12 days) \u2014 adversarial prompt-injection against three sandboxed agents. Paid via Stripe. *Directly uses your agent-harness/gate skills.* Your hand, tonight. **ON-FOCUS**\n2. **ARC Prize 2026 \u2014 up to $2,000,000** \u2014 ARC-AGI-2 (static reasoning) + ARC-AGI-3 (agentic) + $450K Paper Prize. Your QSVC/VQC-on-Hetionet code is the starting artifact; a $20\u201350K paper prize is realistic. Window open \u2192 Nov 2. **ON-FOCUS** \u2014 best fit on the list.\n3. **Mercor \u2014 ~$113/hr** expert eval, $4M/day live payouts, solo, no spend. Fastest to first check. **ON-FOCUS**\n4. **dcode-stack open-sourced** \u2192 Algora bounties + up-to-$100K grants (Block Goose, Codex OSS $25K, NumFOCUS $10K, Together $50K). Monetizes the one unusual thing on your resume. **ON-FOCUS**\n5. **Surge AI \u2014 $200\u2013400/hr** expert eval, but your bar (ML engineer, not PhD/litigator) is likely too high this week \u2014 kept on watch. **ADJACENT**\n6. **Freelance RAG/agent-harness contract work \u2014 ~$185/hr median, $200\u2013600 top** (Toptal/Upwork). Well-fit, bottleneck is client acquisition. **ADJACENT**\n\n**Truly checked-and-empty (not padded):** agent leaderboards (research-only, no cash), Immunefi (Solidity/Rust \u2014 outside the stack), Kaggle general (small prizes), ARC 2025/2024 (closed).\n\n**If I could only move on one thing tonight:** hunt a huntr Objective \u2014 real, paid, 12-day window, your skills on the line. Then this week, score your hybrid-QML code on ARC-AGI-2.\n\n[Revenue Opportunities \u2014 2026-09-01](revenue-2026-09-01.md)", "artifacts": ["revenue-2026-09-01.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-718bba4e0d"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-80b613107c','task-9b2a9d143b',1788311582.72214841,'{"task_id": "task-9b2a9d143b", "run_id": "run-80b613107c", "started_at": 1788311582.7221484, "finished_at": 1788312018.485146, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. `revenue-2026-09-02.md` is written.\n\n**Run #2 summary (2026-09-02):**\n\nThe headline of this run is **correcting my own 09-01 error**, exactly the anti-pattern the job called out. I read the ARC Prize task pages and **ARC-AGI-2 is not knowledge-graph / link-prediction** \u2014 it''s static grid-reasoning under a strict no-API, offline rule. So your QSVC/KG stack does *not* transfer. The honest overlap is **ARC-AGI-3, the interactive-agent track** \u2014 that''s where your OpenWorker stack genuinely belongs.\n\n**Five ranked findings (ON-FOCUS unless noted):**\n1. **huntr \"Inside Job\" $15K** \u2014 ends **Sep 14** (re-verified), humans-only prompt attacks; your agent skills directly.\n2. **ARC Prize 2026 ARC-AGI-3** \u2014 up to **$700K** + **$450K Paper Prize**, open now \u2192 Nov 2, *corrected* to the agent track.\n3. **QHack 2026** (Xanadu/Pennylane) \u2014 **$67K pool / $15K grand**, **Oct 16\u201323**; your PennyLane/Qiskit stack, thin field.\n4. **Ethos Review** \u2014 $35\u2013225/hr expert network, inbound matching (ADJACENT).\n5. **Mercor** \u2014 $113/hr expert eval, live listings (fastest path to first check).\n6. **Apart Research** \u2014 AI-safety + AI-Safety\u00d7Physics hackathons/sprints + fellowship (research, recurring-pay model).\n\n**Corrected from 09-01:** Algora is a *recruiting lead-gen board*, not a bounty board \u2014 flagged it. **Empty this run:** Kaggle (small/per-run only), Aicrowd (no verifiable active competitive prize window), `unitary.foundation` grant pages (404, unverified), `mlcontests.com` (404).\n\n**Carry-forward:** ARC-AGI-2 retired as a fit; XPRIZE Quantum 7 finalists chosen / wildcard closed Mar 4; huntr, Mercor, Ethos still live.\n\nNote: FOCUS.md is still **absent** in the workspace, so tags were assigned by hand \u2014 if it exists elsewhere, re-tag next run.\n\n[Revenue Opportunities \u2014 2026-09-02](revenue-2026-09-02.md)", "artifacts": ["revenue-2026-09-02.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-80b613107c"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-f8da821c9e','task-9b2a9d143b',1788312812.73373746,'{"task_id": "task-9b2a9d143b", "run_id": "run-f8da821c9e", "started_at": 1788312812.7337375, "finished_at": 1788313268.276411, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nRun complete. Both deliverables written: [revenue-2026-09-03.md](revenue-2026-09-03.md) and updated [opportunities.md](opportunities.md).\n\n## What this run delivered\n\n**The headline finding \u2014 the fastest legitimate cash on the entire list was being missed twice, now caught:** the **expert-network big five (GLG / AlphaSights / Guidepoint / Third Bridge / Coleman)**. Your production-ML + RAG + agent-orchestration + quantum-ML profile is exactly what their clients pay **$250\u2013500/hr per call** to ask about. No entity, no spend. I registered this as a first move and added it to the tracker.\n\n**New weekly-pay finds:** **Outlier / Scale AI** (ML/AI track, median **$150/hr, paid weekly, \"actively hiring\"**), **OpenTrain AI** (expert **LLM red-team $100/hr** \u2014 your adversarial-gate muscle, recurring), and **Handshake AI** ($108/hr avg).\n\n**Verified unchanged (not re-reported as fresh):**\n- **huntr \"Inside Job\"** \u2014 still **open, ends Sep 14, 3PM CUT**, $15K pot. Re-verified on the board''s own leaderboard (still contested, live).\n- **ARC Prize 2026** \u2014 open (submissions Nov 2, papers Nov 8). **Still ARC-AGI-3 only**; ARC-AGI-2 retired as a dead fit. The $75K paper prize is the realistic target.\n- **QHack 2026** \u2014 open, window Oct 16\u201323, $67K pool. **Quantum every-run check held.**\n- **Mercor** \u2014 live (24+ pages of current listings).\n- **Algora** \u2014 corrected: still a recruiting board, not a bounty source.\n\n**Continuity maintained:** I did the pre-search read of both prior runs and the tracker, carried every row forward, moved ARC-AGI-2 and Algora into \"closed/never re-report,\" and only searched for what was genuinely new.\n\n**The correction discipline held:** every fit claim states the actual input/output/scoring (e.g., ARC-AGI-3 = agent in a no-API novel environment; ARC-AGI-2 = grid reasoning under a no-API rule \u2014 no overlap with your KG stack).\n\n**Next-hour moves, soonest-cash first:** (1) tonight huntr Objective 1; (2) this hour register on the five expert networks; (3) this week set Outlier + Mercor + OpenTrain profiles live.\n\nNote: FOCUS.md is still absent from the workspace, so findings were hand-tagged ON-FOCUS vs ADJACENT \u2014 if it exists elsewhere, re-tag next run.", "artifacts": ["revenue-2026-09-03.md", "opportunities.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-f8da821c9e"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-d5a6084d88','task-9b2a9d143b',1788315032.75903582,'{"task_id": "task-9b2a9d143b", "run_id": "run-d5a6084d88", "started_at": 1788315032.7590358, "finished_at": 1788315519.5852518, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Fifth run complete \u2014 `revenue-2026-09-04.md` written, `opportunities.md` tracker updated and carried forward.\n\n## What this run found\n\nThe genuinely fresh contribution was the **[RED TEAM & EVAL PROGRAMMES]** track \u2014 standing, recurring AI-lab bounties that recur so \"getting accepted once pays repeatedly.\" This is the closest match to what you do all day, and it''s the one cluster no prior run hit:\n\n1. **Anthropic Model Safety Bug Bounty** (HackerOne, open since May 2026) \u2014 up to **$15K** for a universal jailbreak; **$550K paid across 429 cases** documented. [ASYNC]\n2. **OpenAI Safety Bug Bounty** (Bugcrowd, live from Mar 2026) \u2014 up to **$100K**, $1M annual pool, agentic/MCP scope. [ASYNC]\n3. **Mozilla 0din** \u2014 $500\u2013$15K per LLM finding, open submissions, 3-day triage. [ASYNC]\n4. **Grey Sweep Arena** \u2014 live **Hazard Hunt**, **$20K chemistry wave, 0/10 solved today** (your edge), plus a paid red-team network for standout performers. [ASYNC]\n5. **AfterQuery Project Fenrir** \u2014 security-researcher role, project-based pay. [ASYNC]\n\n## Honest empty/disqualified calls\n- **[COMPUTE CREDITS] \u2192 DISQUALIFIED**: GCP TPU Research Cloud & Google research credits require faculty/PhD/postdoc at an institution. No solo path. Moved to the closed table so the next run stops checking.\n- **[PASSIVE/ARTIFACT] \u2192 THIN/UNVERIFIED**: Replicate = buyer pays, no author payout card; HuggingFace revenue share has no reachable rate card; dataset marketplaces are SEO listicles. Effectively empty for you (distribution/volume problem) \u2014 honest call.\n- **Sigma (trading)**: listed as off-limits, not a clean async product.\n\nThe huntr $15K (ends Sep 14 3PM CUT), ARC, and QHack were re-verified and carried forward unchanged. FOCUS.md is still absent \u2014 tags are hand-assigned.\n\n[Revenue Opportunities \u2014 2026-09-04](revenue-2026-09-04.md)", "artifacts": ["revenue-2026-09-04.md", "opportunities.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-d5a6084d88"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-70a4eb6504','task-1b2c4d3f13',1788336008.82208991,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-70a4eb6504", "started_at": 1788336008.82209, "finished_at": 1788336351.3953943, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. I wrote the deliverable to `papers-2026-09-02.md`.\n\n**What I found (2026-09-02):** 9 new papers, all submitted 2026-09-01 (the 2609.0xxx series, which didn''t exist on 09-01).\n\n**ON-FOCUS (4):**\n- **2609.01448** Verifiable quantum advantage at extremely low depth \u2014 a shallow QNC\u2070[loglog] circuit solves a classically-hard sampling problem that a plain classical computer can verify, no mid-circuit measurement needed. This is the \"near-term noisy QPU already beats classical\" half of the OpenEvolve Phase-3 QM question (changed state: today''s lead is a hardware-advantage result, not another QEC/decoder number).\n- **2609.01481** Harness-of-Harness \u2014 a real multi-day autonomous coding loop (70+ iterations, +52% average gain) whose whole point is making improvement auditable. The positive counterpart to the 08-31 RSI ladder + EvoSkill red-team.\n- **2609.01487** Defense-as-Skill \u2014 makes the runtime guard the *same installable skill-as-attack* artifact, closing the trust hole 2608.30429 opened on 08-31 (new state, not re-stated).\n- **2609.01600** CordisBench \u2014 LMs degrade at reasoning about self-modifying harness components as complexity grows; the first quantified test of \"can the model be trusted to change the harness that constrains it.\"\n\n**ADJACENT (3):** 2609.01605 (depth-1 unitary expanders + optimal entanglement-gap relation), 2609.01449 (diffusion-as-training-curriculum anytime solver), 2609.01573 (near-optimal SFT-RL budget allocation transferring small\u2192large).\n\nAll prior 2608.31xxx/2608.285xx clusters are marked carried-forward, not re-reported. I also noted the state change to the paper-watch brain thread.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-09-02.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-70a4eb6504"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-4cd51a941a','task-f471043f3e',1788336908.83489799,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-4cd51a941a", "started_at": 1788336908.834898, "finished_at": 1788337358.233775, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote `breakage-2026-09-02.md`.\n\n**What I found:** One item genuinely moved \u2014 and it''s the top-risk one, not a new break.\n\n- **TheRock #7051 (gfx1151 AsyncEventsLoop 100%-CPU-spin) received its first activity since 08-13: a 5th comment today, 2026-09-01 22:27** by leapdragon. It extends to a *second spin class* (`InterruptSignal::WaitRelaxed` livelock, one-per-TP-rank, appears with RCCL), a *second GPU family* (Navi 21 / gfx1030, 4\u00d7 Radeon PRO V620), and a bounded-backoff patch under AMD review. Still `open / triage` \u2014 no fix. Critically, the issue''s own reproduced matrix **puts your 7.13.0-nightly wheel inside the affected 1.21 family**, so this is on your own `torch 2.11.0+rocm7.13.0` line, not just a future one. Suggested 30-second check: `strings` your bundled `libhsa-runtime64.so` \u2014 1.21 = affected, 1.18 = clean.\n- **`legacy-rocm-build #6522` unchanged** (open/triage/last-08-10), now framed upstream as the same family.\n- **Everything else confirmed unchanged** via the GitHub API: ollama v0.33.2 (ROCm wheel still shipped), llama.cpp v0.3.0/b10621, OpenWorker v0.2.1, unsloth v0.1.804-beta, **transformers v5.16.1**.\n- **Correction:** a `web_search` snippet claimed transformers v5.6.0 was released \u2014 **it''s not real** (`releases/latest` = v5.16.1, the v5.6.0 tag URL 404s). I disregarded it.\n\n**Budget note:** Tavily was **back up this run** for the first time in 8 consecutive runs (the `EAI_AGAIN` block is broken) \u2014 4/5 queries returned, all within the 6-search cap, so this run discovered leads via Tavily rather than just verifying via API. Context7 still not exercised. No break introduced on the box; the single movement is the top gfx1151 runtime risk getting richer and landing on your own wheel line.", "artifacts": ["breakage-2026-09-02.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-4cd51a941a"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-7185b6ec53','task-c6cf366b90',1788338108.8528161,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-7185b6ec53", "started_at": 1788338108.852816, "finished_at": 1788338377.9775167, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. This run''s real work was deadline re-verification, not new searching \u2014 and the finding matters: **the two most urgent, high-fitting targets are already drafted and have hard deadlines that are about to close.**\n\n**What I found:** I re-verified all 7 drafted programmes live against their official pages today. **Two are OPEN with near-term deadlines that are the real priority:**\n- **Cambridge ERA:AI Fellowship \u2014 OPEN, closes Sep 13, 11:59pm AoE (12 days left).** The no-PhD / talent-first bar matches the resume unusually well via the hybrid QML project. The honest gate is the 10-week UK logistics.\n- **MATS Residency (Winter 2027) \u2014 OPEN, closes Oct 31.** Same QML \"build-then-verify\" discipline + self-taught path fit the program''s explicit no-PhD bar.\n\nThe other open ones (ADF, CTEC, CSC, and Lila \u2014 though Lila has a degree bar) are rolling and should be filed early. GovAI and AIAF are confirmed closed for the year. The only genuinely new live finding was **DoorDash AI Research Fellowship** (paid SF-based), which I reported but did not draft because its stated bar is PhD-track.\n\nI rewrote `opportunities.md` (carried forward, re-verified, IAPS added as closed) and wrote the shortlist to `jobs-2026-09-02.md`. No new drafts were created \u2014 the top matches were all drafted in the 09-01 runs, and this run confirms they''re all still live and applicable. The run''s headline message to the applicant: **the priority right now is to actually file the ERA:AI and MATS applications, not to generate another shortlist.**", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-09-02.md", "opportunities.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-7185b6ec53"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-5e7be62b54','task-c685e22a0b',1788340808.89184188,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-5e7be62b54", "started_at": 1788340808.891842, "finished_at": 1788341062.4567313, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Briefing written to `morning-briefing-2026-09-02.md`.\n\nThree things genuinely moved since your Sept 1 briefing: the freshest tracked frontier model is now **Qwen3.8-Max-0902 (Qwen, Sep 2)**, superseding my carried GLM-5.3-Flash baseline; **Anthropic shipped Claude Fable 5.1 / Mythos 5.1 on Sep 1** with a ~75% cache-price cut and Terminal-Bench-Science jumping from 24.7 to 52.6; and \u2014 closest to your box \u2014 **ROCm 10 has gone GA (~Aug 28)** with **explicit Strix Halo support**, vLLM+SGLang, and the ROCm.AI toolchain, so your ROCm baseline of 7.2.2 is now upgradeable. The four ADJACENT world-macro items (global bond selloff to 2008-high yields, the continuing Iran/Hormuz gas thread, Google''s 88%-token Gemini video analysis, and the Anthropic \"Astra\"/EFS safety notes) are tagged ADJACENT and none touch the repo-only FOCUS projects. One flag: I couldn''t open a primary source for Qwen3.8-Max-0902''s specs or the \"Astra\" details, so those are held out rather than cited. Two DuckDuckGo calls failed and were re-run via Tavily; budget came in well under the 5-search/4-fetch cap.", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-09-02.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-5e7be62b54"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-8910dd56e3','task-78fcb8b740',1788342308.90401959,'{"task_id": "task-78fcb8b740", "run_id": "run-8910dd56e3", "started_at": 1788342308.9040196, "finished_at": 1788342588.5805929, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote **`outside-view-2026-09-02.md`** in the workspace.\n\nTarget I argued against: the **agpack \"verifiable-agent harness\" build itself** (FOCUS Active #1, P0 = \"ship it\"), with its portability proof (`proof.py` / `DeterministicFingerprintDriver`) as the credibility linchpin.\n\nThe core line: agpack is building the whole agent OS from scratch (Steps 1\u20135), but the field''s own evidence says the value and the moat are moving *out* of the bespoke harness. The sharpest attack is the one you already raised about yourself \u2014 your 2026-08-30 honest caveat admits the portability proof is **not** a true cross-engine test, and arXiv:2509.11068 empirically shows LLM determinism breaks across GPUs, so the linchpin asserts cross-engine determinism it never varied and can''t prove. I argued you should abandon the portability-proof-as-linchpin and redirect that effort into the one gate the current build is silent on: **silent-error / statement-fabrication fraud** (arXiv:2607.15684 \u2014 42% of AR bugs are silent; fabricating completion is 90% silent), plus reuse a pre-built behavioral-contract + drift benchmark (AgentAssert / AgentContract-Bench) instead of reinventing Conformance Tier B. One cheap, falsifiable experiment is included: re-run passing bundles under a perturbed environment / real second interpreter and feed fabricated runs through the current gate.\n\nCaveat I stated plainly in the file: I could not open the agpack source (path outside my accessible roots), so the target and its structure come from FOCUS.md and your 2026-08-30 memory record, not source I directly verified.", "artifacts": ["outside-view-2026-09-02.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-8910dd56e3"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-1763f06a88','task-ecad448aa3',1788343208.91437172,'{"task_id": "task-ecad448aa3", "run_id": "run-1763f06a88", "started_at": 1788343208.9143717, "finished_at": 1788344164.6684868, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nAll outputs verified. The 2026-09-02 ingest run is complete.\n\n## Done \u2014 2026-09-02 KB ingest\n\n**What changed:** Stored **12 net-new findings** to the Qdrant KB (9 ON-FOCUS + 3 ADJACENT), growing `default` from **60 \u2192 72** points. Read 6 source files, found 8 net-new in breakage/agents and 1 each in jobs/outside-view/morning-briefing, then stored.\n\n**Check that ran and passed:**\n- Stored 12, skipped 0, 0 duplicates (`indexing script` + `ingest_kb_2026-09-02.json`: 12 IDs).\n- Retrievability verified: all 12 new points read back via **`scroll`** (the `/points/query` endpoint still rejects every vector shape \u2014 `size` 384/768/72/256 all fail), correct `document`/`metadata` payload. `indexed_vectors_count: 0` is expected \u2014 HNSW is lazy.\n- Mandated running total: `points_count: 72`.\n\n**Findings landed:** 4 papers (2609.01448 log-log quantum advantage, Harness-of-Harness +52% dev loop, SkillSonar closes 2608.30429, CordisBench); TheRock #7051 **5th comment** (5th \u2014 second spin class, Navi 21 GPU family, on host''s 7.13.0-nightly wheel); transformers v5.6.0 false lead (real latest v5.16.1); DoorDash AI Research Fellowship; agpack portability-proof critique + AgentContract-Bench prior art; 3 adjacent news (Qwen3.8-Max-0902, ROCm 10, Claude Fable 5.1).\n\n**Deliverables:** `knowledge/ingest/2026-09-02.md` (ledger), `knowledge/report-2026-09-02.md`, `knowledge/threads/{local-stack-breakage,automation-fleet,agpack}.md` extended with movement + the adversarial outside view citing 2509.11068/2607.15684.\n\n**Not stored (per mandate):** everything 09-01 already stored (re-verified unchanged); `repo-activity` 0 net-new (gateway reachable but token dead on all 10 repos \u2014 `Bad credentials`, last verifiable brief 2026-08-24); thin out-of-body notes (no primary source); PII.\n\n**Blocked/flagged:** the **GitHub MCP gateway token is fully dead** \u2014 reachable but `Bad credentials` on all 10 repos incl. the public liaison-agentSystem. I recorded this in the KB and the `automation-fleet` thread rather than re-reading repo activity, since it''s unverifiable from primary source. No open questions needing your decision \u2014 the run''s mandate was satisfied within budget (12/25 stores, 0 finds, today''s files stored-direct).", "artifacts": ["store_2026-09-02.py", "ingest_kb_2026-09-02.json", "report-2026-09-02.md", "ledger-2026-09-02.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-1763f06a88"}');
