INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-bf503adabe','task-f471043f3e',1788365705.53868269,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-bf503adabe", "started_at": 1788365705.5386827, "finished_at": 1788366163.7521203, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote **`breakage-2026-09-03.md`** to the workspace.\n\n**What I found (vs. 09-02, which is now stale):**\n\nThe one net-new move is **unsloth v0.1.804-beta \u2192 v0.1.806-beta** (published 2026-09-02 12:48 UTC) \u2014 and it''s the on-FOCUS AMD/gfx1151 item. But it''s the **Desktop-app release**, not the torch training path, and its \"Strengthened AMD/ROCm detection\" body (plus context7 confirming `is_rdna()` now supports gfx1151) does **not** change the CUDA-substitution posture \u2014 the reinstall guardrail from 08-26 still stands.\n\nEverything else is unchanged from 09-02:\n- **TheRock #7051** (top gfx1151 runtime risk) \u2014 open/triage/5 comments, last touched 2026-09-01, no merge, no movement.\n- **legacy-rocm-build #6522** \u2014 open/triage/3 comments, last 2026-08-10, no fix.\n- torch 2.11.0+rocm7.13.0 unchanged on host (ecosystem on 2.12.0/nightly 2.13.0); ollama v0.33.2 (ROCm wheel still shipped); llama.cpp v0.3.0/b10621 (net-new compile-bug lead is an existing ROCm-7.2 rocwmma fragility, not this box); OpenWorker v0.2.1; transformers v5.16.1 (the v5.6.0 \"release\" is a false lead \u2014 tag 404s); LibreChat unverifiable/no change.\n- New informational adjacent: **Ubuntu 26.04 LTS now officially lists gfx1151** as supported ROCm hardware (not a host change).\n\n**Budget/statement:** Tavily was **UP** (first time since the 8-run EAI_AGAIN block; 4/4 used) and **context7 was also up** this run \u2014 first live context7 read since 09-02. All version-of-record facts verified directly via the GitHub REST API; nothing reconstructed from memory.\n\nI updated memory with the tool recovery (tavily + context7 back up), since it changes how future scheduled runs of this job can run.", "artifacts": ["breakage