INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-9a6818a76b','task-1b2c4d3f13',1788422406.04420638,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-9a6818a76b", "started_at": 1788422406.0442064, "finished_at": 1788423122.0478847, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone \u2014 the brief is written and the record updated.\n\nThis run''s arXiv MCP server was down at session start (transient gateway outage, distinct from the known 09-02 credential/search blocks), so I queried arXiv''s own Atom API through the `web_fetch` read tool \u2014 same data source, no shell/curl. Picked 6 papers submitted 2026-09-02, all new vs yesterday''s 09-02 report.\n\n**What I found** \u2014 3 ON-FOCUS, 3 ADJACENT, all on the recurring theme that \"the structure around the model is the load-bearing lever, and it must be auditable/reversible/grounded\":\n\n- **Quantum (ON-FOCUS):** 2609.02641 \u2014 a spin-qubit *shuttling bus* that co-designs syndrome extraction + transversal gates to arbitrary logical qubits + 15-to-1 magic-state distillation, the \"one real QPU platform can run the full fault-tolerant stack\" half of the OpenEvolve Phase-3 QM question. Plus 3 ADJACENT (parallel QAE w/o power-of-two ladder, long-haul network polarization stabilization, auditable-deployed-QML classifier).\n- **ML (ON-FOCUS):** 2609.02749 Repo-To-Skill/DisCo \u2014 distilling 1,000 ML repos into 5,000+ verified skills yields **+134% MLE-bench under a fixed agent**, the reuse-of-verified-knowledge pole of OpenEvolve''s AI-for-Science loop. Plus 3 ADJACENT (Cliff first-mismatch reward shaping, Declarative Attention, Nemotron IOI).\n- **RSI (ON-FOCUS):** 2609.02786 SafeEvolve \u2014 a *self-evolving harness made auditable AND reversible*, the OpenWorker \"trust-the-loop-but-see-the-failure\" open question as a working architecture. Plus ADJACENT 2609.02750 Bilevel Coordinated Reflection, which *proves* a transcript-only gate cannot certify progress.\n\nWrote **`papers-2026-09-03.md`** to the workspace and recorded 6 new IDs (with the OpenEvolve/OpenWorker continuity notes) to the paper-watch memory thread so the next run builds on this rather than rediscovering it.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-09-03.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-9a6818a76b"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-5069dc5de1','task-c6cf366b90',1788424506.06758356,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-5069dc5de1", "started_at": 1788424506.0675836, "finished_at": 1788425020.2977135, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Three files written to the workspace: `jobs-2026-09-03.md`, `drafts/cover-letter-GovAI-seasonal-fellow.md`, `drafts/resume-tweaks-GovAI-seasonal-fellow.md`, plus a rewritten `opportunities.md`.\n\n**What I found (2026-09-03 run):**\n\nThe run''s job was deadline-re-verification + a freshness search, so the headline is mostly \"still-open, now clock-tight.\"\n\n**The two hard deadlines \u2014 both still OPEN, now closer:**\n- **Cambridge ERA:AI** \u2014 confirmed live today, closes **Sep 13 11:59pm AoE** (~10 days left). Most pressing open deadline, already drafted.\n- **MATS Residency** \u2014 confirmed live today (`matsprogram.org/residency`), closes **Oct 31 2026 AoE** (~7.5 weeks), already drafted.\n\n**Genuinely new this run \u2014 GovAI opened a fresh window.** The 2026 Research Fellowship call is still closed, but GovAI today has **two new requisitions** live on `governance.ai/opportunities`: **DC Research Manager (deadline Sep 13 11:59pm ET)** and **Research Manager, UK Fellowships (deadline Sep 27 11:59pm BST)** \u2014 3-month seasonal-fellowship *management* roles. These are a stretch vs. the applied-research profile, so I drafted one tailored letter framed as the **Applied-track fellow** seat and flagged the manager-vs-fellow distinction honestly in both the cover letter and the resume-tweaks.\n\n**Nothing genuinely new on the standard-role surface** (all were drafted 09-01: Valtech, Further, Stellar, ICONMA, Bybit, GCP Engineer). **DoorDash AI Research Fellowship** re-checked \u2014 still open, still a strong-PhD bar, reported only. **Anthropic Fellows / OpenAI Safety Fellowship** remain correctly bucketed to the grant digest.\n\n**The run''s verdict:** everything live is open and applicable, but the highest-leverage move is to actually **file ERA:AI (Sep 13) and MATS (Oct 31)** \u2014 both open, high-fitting, and already drafted \u2014 rather than generate another shortlist.", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-09-03.md", "opportunities.md", "drafts/cover-letter-GovAI-seasonal-fellow.md", "drafts/resume-tweaks-GovAI-seasonal-fellow.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-5069dc5de1"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-040f91cbcd','task-c685e22a0b',1788427206.09299159,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-040f91cbcd", "started_at": 1788427206.0929916, "finished_at": 1788427493.5873895, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote **`morning-briefing-2026-09-03.md`**.\n\nWhat genuinely moved in the last 24h: Google launched **Gemini 3.8 Flash (Sep 3)** \u2014 its best coding/reasoning model yet at the same $0.75/$3.75 pricing, with a gated \"Cyber\" model \u2014 topping the Qwen3.8-Max-0902 / Fable 5.1 layers I''d carried through Sep 2. **Meta''s Muse Spark 1.3 (Sep 2)** tied the frontier (AA Index 61) at the cheapest-per-task price, landing squarely in the EU AI Act open-weights debate. Macro **de-escalated** rather than escalated \u2014 Trump hinted the Iran campaign would be \"short-lived,\" oil slipped (Brent ~$95.20, WTI ~$90.77), and 10-year yields dipped, a fresh turn on the Hormuz run I''ve carried since Aug 25. Local-inference had **no fresh 24h drop** (your ROCm 10 GA from Sep 2 is still the last real box-relevant one), though I carried a Strix Halo speculative-decoding tuning tip. No bullets bear on the repo-only FOCUS projects \u2014 all tagged ADJACENT. Budget: 5 searches, 4 fetches.", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-09-03.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-040f91cbcd"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-b107f6287c','task-9b2a9d143b',1788428706.103096,'{"task_id": "task-9b2a9d143b", "run_id": "run-b107f6287c", "started_at": 1788428706.103096, "finished_at": 1788429083.3350043, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. **`revenue-latest.md`** is written (overwriting every prior run), ordered by time to first payment.\n\n**What changed since the 09-04 run \u2014 one real finding, the rest carry-forward:**\n\n- **Genuinely new: Apart Research AI Incident Response Sprint** \u2014 its **$2,000 cash prize pool was just now verified** (09-04 had it marked UNVERIFIED). It''s solo/online, ends **Sep 13**, and its **Containment track is literally the dcode-stack gate reframed as the grading rubric** (\"a third party verifies compliance without access to the lab''s network\"). Highest-fit entry on the list; promoted to a full ranked entry, tagged ON-FOCUS.\n- **ARC-AGI-3: Milestone #2 (Sep 30) has now passed** \u2014 called out explicitly so no run re-derives it as still open. Grand Prize + Paper Prize (Nov 2/8) remain live.\n- **Grey Sweep** rolled from the old single chemistry wave to a rolling **four-category Hazard Hunt ($20K/cat) + new IPI Lucky Break** \u2014 re-verified as live, different composition.\n- **huntr** (Sep 14 3PM CUT), **QHack** (Oct 16\u201323), **Mercor**, and the Anthropic/OpenAI/0din standing bounties all re-verified live vs. primary sources.\n\n**What was honestly empty (so the next run skips them):** Open-Source Bounties \u2014 no fresh solo-mergeable issue; Compute Credits \u2014 still requires an institution (the 09-04 GCP/Google finding, not re-checked); Sell-an-Artifact \u2014 Replicate is pay-as-you-go to the buyer, HF revenue share has no reachable author rate card.\n\nTwo things I won''t bury: **FOCUS.md is still absent** from the workspace (I hand-tagged ON-FOCUS/ADJACENT), and the **Apart prize note is staged under \"## NEW - CARRIES A DEADLINE\"** at the top of the file so it can be folded into the read-only