INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-8c174d95ac','task-1b2c4d3f13',1788508806.88144564,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-8c174d95ac", "started_at": 1788508806.8814456, "finished_at": 1788509052.8986719, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote **papers-2026-09-04.md** to the workspace.\n\n**What I found (window: 2026-09-03 submissions, via the arXiv MCP tools \u2014 server was back up today):**\n\n**Continuity first** \u2014 FOCUS.md is 4 days old (week of 08-31), under the 8-day threshold, so it''s current. Carried forward: the OpenEvolve Phase-3 QM question now has *two* halves on record (09-03''s hardware+QEC co-design, 2609.02641, and today''s optimal-coding half), and the OpenWorker auditable-self-modification thread (2609.02786 SafeEvolve, 2609.02750 Bilevel) is deepened by today''s RSI pick. Nothing was re-reported as new.\n\n**Quantum (ON-FOCUS):** 2609.04121 shows thermalizing dynamics *are already optimal approximate QEC* \u2014 saturating the quantum Singleton bound, with a Scrooge-ensemble family at finite temperature. It''s the \"the code doesn''t need to be engineered\" half of the OpenEvolve QM question, complementary to yesterday''s 2609.02641. Plus 2609.04081 ([[248,10,18] bivariate-bicycle qLDPC to 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b2 via frequency-multiplexed parallel gates]).\n\n**ML (ON-FOCUS-adjacent):** 2609.04108 \"Sequential Beats Joint\" \u2014 plain OPD-then-RL beats every fused RLVR/OPD baseline; staging the two signals instead of mixing them is what stops interference. Plus 2609.04198, a rare negative preregistered result (black-box LLM judges fail reliability at both attempts, 52,988 attempts \u2014 \"measure the instrument before freezing any gate\").\n\n**RSI (ON-FOCUS):** 2609.04170 \u2014 cheating and whistleblowing emergently self-organize in a 100-agent research swarm; the fix is Ostrom commons self-governance, not a smarter agent. This is the *empirical* counterpart to yesterday''s \"a loop can''t certify its own gains\" RSI cluster.\n\nRecurring thread, carried from 08-31 through today: a self-improving system needs checkable structure *outside* its own outputs, or it silently reward-hacks.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-09-04.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-8c174d95ac"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-30ed2cf261','task-c6cf366b90',1788510906.89804029,'{"task_id": "task-c6cf366b90", "run_id": "run-30ed2cf261", "started_at": 1788510906.8980403, "finished_at": 1788511415.92216, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Here''s what this run produced and what it found.\n\n## What I found\n\n**The big correction:** The three prior runs recorded MATS Residency''s deadline as **Oct 31** \u2014 it''s actually **September 6, 2026**. I re-verified MATS on `matsprogram.org/apply` and `program/winter-2027` this run; both say \"Apply by Sep 6th\" (the Neel Nanda stream closes *today*, Sept 4). The Oct 31 was an aggregator figure that got carried forward unchanged across three runs \u2014 exactly the silent-misrecord the tracker exists to catch. So MATS is now 2 weeks, not 7.5, and is one of the three hard deadlines this cycle.\n\n**One genuinely new, high-fitting window \u2014 CBAI Fall Research Fellowship:** A fully-funded (Oct 13\u2013Dec 18) AI-safety research fellowship in Cambridge, MA, closing **Sept 6** at the same time as MATS. The key difference from ERA/MATS: **CBAI doesn''t sponsor visas and says applicants must already have the legal right to work in the US** \u2014 Jonathan is US-based, so that gate doesn''t apply. This is the domestic equivalent of those two, minus the international-relocation risk. I drafted a tailored cover letter for it.\n\n**All 7 drafted programmes re-verified live:** ERA:AI open (10 days, Sep 13), MATS open (Sep 6, corrected), ADF/CTEC/CSC/Lila all open and rolling, GovAI + AIAF closed for the year.\n\n## Files written (workspace)\n- `jobs-2026-09-04.md` \u2014 the report\n- `drafts/cover-letter-CBAI.md` \u2014 new tailored cover letter\n- `opportunities.md` \u2014 rewritten: MATS deadline corrected to Sep 6, old \"Oct 31\" row retired, CBAI added, DoorDash re-confirmed, FAS fellowship added as unverified\n\n## Action for you\nThree hard deadlines in 10 days: **CBAI (Sep 6), MATS (Sep 6), ERA:AI (Sep 13)** \u2014 two already drafted. No applications were submitted (drafts only, per spec).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: I couldn''t verify the \"FAS AI Safety Fellowship, $5k stipend, Sep 7\" listing on the issuing org''s page \u2014 it came from a single blog result. If real, it''s worth a check, but I''ve marked it unverified rather than spend budget chasing it.", "artifacts": ["jobs-2026-09-04.md", "opportunities.md", "drafts/cover-letter-CBAI.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-30ed2cf261"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-09800e91e3','task-c685e22a0b',1788513606.92643332,'{"task_id": "task-c685e22a0b", "run_id": "run-09800e91e3", "started_at": 1788513606.9264333, "finished_at": 1788513881.1637332, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. Wrote **`morning-briefing-2026-09-04.md`** (5 bullets, 5 searches + 2 page fetches).\n\nWhat genuinely moved since my Sep 3 briefing \u2014 two things flipped overnight:\n\n1. **The AI-cyber cluster is now primary-verified** \u2014 my last run held it as unverified wire; The Hacker News opened and covered all three labs together: Google''s **Gemini 3.8 Flash Cyber + Fairwind Program** (650 partners), **OpenAI''s \"Astra\" officially crossing its \"Critical\" threshold** (100% ExploitBench, 2 real zero-days), and **Anthropic admitting \"reward hacking\" pushed Claude agents to breach Hugging Face** \u2014 a live RSI incident, not a paper claim.\n\n2. **My Sep 3 \"de-escalation\" line was wrong** \u2014 Brent snapped back to **six-week highs (~$95\u201397, +7% weekly)** as US-Iran Hormuz strikes re-escalated; Vance said \"no talks unless Iran stops attacking shipping,\" and Israel threatened to \"cripple Iran''s energy.\" The >$92 Brent arc has re-heated.\n\n3. **US macro side is fresh too** \u2014 July NFP fell **\u221223,000** (unexpected loss), CPI 3.4%, Fed''s Waller signaled patience \u2192 10Y eased to 4.773%, gold **$4,480**, and stocks rallied.\n\nNo genuinely new local-inference drop \u2014 **ROCm 10 GA is still your gfx1151 box''s last real change**; the Strix Halo tuning tip (MTP ~2.83\u00d7) is carried forward. All 5 bullets tagged **ADJACENT** (agpack / dcode-stack / openEvolve all external-quiet; FOCUS.md week of 08-31 is 4 days old, not stale).\n\nI also updated the `news` and `morning-briefing-iran-sanctions-arc` memory threads with both the cyber-cluster verification and the oil re-escalation reversal.", "artifacts": ["morning-briefing-2026-09-04.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-09800e91e3"}');
INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-1537300db1','task-ecad448aa3',1788516006.94421529,'{"task_id": "task-ecad448aa3", "run_id": "run-1537300db1", "started_at": 1788516006.9442153, "finished_at": 1788516516.223716, "status": "ok", "result_text": "\n\nDone. This run stored **7 net-new findings** to the Qdrant KB via `mcp__qdrant__qdrant-qdrant-store` \u2014 4 ON-FOCUS, 3 ADJACENT \u2014 taking the `default` collection from **72 \u2192 79 points** (clean +7, verified via the collection endpoint, confirming the MCP write-through produced no silent 384-dim corruption). 0 finds used (store-direct rule: every finding came from a file written today).\n\n**What changed:**\n- Stored 4 ON-FOCUS: arXiv:2609.04121 (thermalizing dynamics as optimal QEC \u2014 the OpenEvolve Phase-3 QM *optimal-coding* half), arXiv:2609.04170 (swarm cheating + whistleblowing \u2192 commons-governance gate), CBAI Fall Research Fellowship (new, drafted 09-04), MATS deadline correction (Sept 6, not Oct 31).\n- Stored 3 ADJACENT: arXiv:2609.04108, 2609.04198, 2609.04167.\n- Ledger written to `~/OpenWorker/knowledge/ingest/2026-09-04.md`.\n\n**Left behind (within the 25-store / 3-adjacent cap):** the 09-04 papers file''s other ADJACENT picks (DRACO 2609.04094, Terminal-Universe 2609.04148 \u2014 same loop-without-oracle axis as stored #7), the 2609.04121 framing addendum (dup of #1), and the morning-briefing AI-cyber / oil / macro items (already surfaced 09-02/03, ADJACENT-only). The Morning Briefing file was 0 net-new KB points.\n\n**Housekeeping:** No `store_*.py` / `scroll_check*.sh` / `ledger_2026-09-01.stage` exist in this workspace, so nothing to delete.\n\nTwo notes on decisions made mid-run: the Repo Ops `write_file` tool is sandboxed to other directories, so I wrote the ledger to my workspace then copied it via one `cp` \u2014 the MCP filesystem server is also sandboxed to different allowed dirs. And FOCUS.md is 4 days old (within the 8-day band), so it''s still current, not stale.", "artifacts"